  "body": "What happens: /merge-ready offered PRs #1824 and #1825 in a merge batch. The only merge-ready label and the only pr-reviewer markers on them were the author's own. No independent review counted. MainSession merged them on 2026-11-15T09:52Z. See the PR comments for the retro reviews that followed.\n\nExpected: /merge-ready offers a PR only when a counted collaborator review exists that is independent of the author (AGENTS.md \"Only collaborators' reviews count\": the review must come from an agent that did not write the change). An author-set merge-ready label on the author's own PR does not meet this.\n\nEvidence: gh api repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/pulls/1824/reviews is empty; the merge-ready label events show actor mkinney (2026-11-15T09:28:11Z), the author himself.\n\nFix: the merge-ready skill's plan step must read pulls/N/reviews and the label-setter (timeline labeled event) per PR, and skip plus report any PR whose only marker source is the author.\n\nDone means: a merge-plan run over PRs that carry only author markers lists them as \"no counted review - not offered\", and a test or worked example in the skill pins it.\n",
